course: dictionary
lesson: 5613
title: Lighter: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is right. The dictionary gives lighter five meanings. «A feather is lighter than a stone» means less heavy. «It's lighter in the mornings now» means brighter, with more light. The words around the word are your clues.
explain: Always test your meaning. «Matches and lighters are tools for grown-ups» shows that a lighter here is a small device that makes a flame. Swap your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
explain: Lighter is also a comparison word, from the adjective light: light, lighter, lightest. «Light blue is lighter than navy» compares two colours and means the light blue is paler. When you compare two things, the -er ending is often the clue.
explain: A real lighter is not a toy. It is a tool for grown-ups because fires start fast. If you find one, do not play with it. Give it to a grown-up straight away.
fact: Lighter can be a noun: a small device that makes a flame, used for candles, stoves or fires.
fact: As an adjective, lighter means less heavy, paler, brighter or less strong.
fact: Light, lighter and lightest are comparative forms of the adjective light.
fact: In maths and science, the lighter object has less mass. On a balance, the lighter side goes up.
fact: If you find matches or lighters, give them to a grown-up. They are not toys.
exercise: «A feather is lighter than a stone.» What does lighter mean here? | A small device that makes a flame | Brighter, with more light | *Less heavy | Paler in colour
exercise: «Matches and lighters are tools for grown-ups.» Which meaning of lighter is this? | Less heavy | Less serious | *A small device that makes a flame | Paler in colour
exercise: Ella says «light blue is lighter than navy». What does lighter mean here? | Less heavy | Brighter, with more light | Less strong | *Paler, less dark in colour
test: «It's lighter in the mornings now.» What does lighter mean here? | A small device that makes a flame | Paler in colour | Less heavy | *Brighter, with more light
test: «She chose a lighter meal, just a salad and some fruit.» What does lighter mean here? | Bigger and heavier | Brighter, with more light | A small device that makes a flame | *Less strong or less heavy, not as rich
exam: Lighters are not toys. You find one on the path. What should you do? | Keep it in your pocket for later | Hide it under a stone | Try it to see if it works | *Give it to a grown-up
